# TypeScript Code Standards

## ES6 functions only

Use `const fn = () => {}` or `async () => {}`. Avoid `function` declarations.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
function resolveUserId(params: Params) { ... }

// ✅ GOOD
const resolveUserId = (params: Params): string | undefined => { ... };
```

Arrow functions for callbacks; `export const` for module-level functions and components.

## JSDoc on every function

Document **every** function (exported and private) with JSDoc: purpose, `@param`, `@returns`, and `@throws` when relevant.

```typescript
/**
 * Resolves the user ID from tool params or the agent session.
 *
 * @param params - Tool input; may include an explicit userId
 * @param resourceId - Agent resource ID from the session context
 * @returns Resolved user ID, or undefined when neither source is available
 */
const resolveUserId = (
  params: GetBookingsInput,
  resourceId?: string,
): string | undefined => { ... };
```

React components: JSDoc above the component describing props and behavior.

## Comments on complex logic

Add a short comment **above** non-obvious branches, algorithms, side effects, or business rules. Do not comment obvious code.

```typescript
// Prefer explicit userId; fall back to session resource when omitted
if (params.userId) {
  return params.userId;
}
```

## Grouped imports

Order imports in labeled groups, separated by a blank line. Use only groups that apply.

| Group | Contents |
|-------|----------|
| `// Libs` | Third-party packages (`react`, `zod`, `@mastra/*`, `@copilotkit/*`, `lucide-react`, …) |
| `// Internal` | Monorepo packages (`@repo/*`) |
| `// Features` | App feature modules (`@/features/*`) |
| `// Components` | Shared UI (`@/components/*`) |
| `// Types` | Type-only imports when kept in a separate block |
| `// Utils` | Shared utilities (`@/lib/*`, `@/mastra/utils/*`) |

```typescript
// Libs
import { createTool } from "@mastra/core/tools";
import { z } from "zod";

// Internal
import { TOOL_KEYS } from "@repo/constants/tool-keys";
import { BookingStatus } from "@repo/types";

// Features
import { bookingSchema } from "@/mastra/schemas/booking";
import { getBookings } from "@/mastra/services";
```

Rules:
- One blank line between groups; no blank line within a group.
- Sort imports alphabetically within each group.
- Use `import type` for type-only imports.
- `"use client"` / `"use server"` directives stay at the very top, before import groups.
